From b80731610e3319d32b91f926205008307ead9010 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Livio Gamassia <livio.gamassia@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 04:43:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(brief): locate the lines of a setting and the tests of a
 topic (#906)

A question about a setting ("what port does the dev server use", "which
env vars change this") or about tests ("which tests cover redirect
handling") has no symbol to resolve, so the region pack showed the wrong
files. The locators search the prompt's content words by line shape (a
constant, an upper-case assignment, a key given a literal, an environment
read, a flag, a default; or a test declaration), rank the rows by the words
the repository does not overuse, and add exact numbered source to the pack:
the setting with its doc comment, the environment variables read, the
matching tests by name with their first lines and the command that runs
only them.

Evidence::grep sends a regular expression as it is. Receipt::weight_of
exposes the relevance probe's weight of a stem. The decision log counts the
located blocks (pack_located).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
